course: dictionary
lesson: 13346
title: Working out a word from clues
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: You do not need to know every word to understand a text. When you meet a new word, read the words around it. They are its context, and they leave clues. «Mia's new hairdo had long curls and a big pink bow.» Curls and a bow are things you can have in your hair, so hairdo must mean a style of hair.
explain: «The wind ruined Sam's hairdo just before the school photo.» Ruined tells you a hairdo can be spoiled, and that it is something you can look neat or messy in. Always ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Some words sound like ordinary words but mean something more exact. Hair is the hair on your head. A hairdo is the way that hair has been cut and styled, especially a special or fancy style. «Grandma's fancy hairdo was pinned with tiny pearls for the wedding.» When context is not enough, a dictionary settles it.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: Context clues can help you work out the meaning of an unknown word.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: «Hairdo» means the way someone's hair is cut and styled, especially a special or fancy style.
fact: «Hairdo» is an informal word, friendly and a little old-fashioned, often used for weddings, parties or school photos.
fact: Phrases: a new hairdo, a fancy hairdo.
exercise: «Mia's new hairdo had long curls and a big pink bow.» What is a hairdo? | A hat worn on sunny days | A pink bow for a present | * The way someone's hair is cut and styled | A kind of shoe
exercise: «The wind ruined Sam's hairdo just before the school photo.» Find and copy one word that tells you a hairdo can be spoiled. | photo | * ruined | school | wind
exercise: Lily says «hairdo» is mid, just say «hair». Why might a writer choose hairdo? | It means a hat | It means exactly the same as hair, so there is no reason to pick it | * It means a particular style, not just hair | It is a longer word
test: «Grandma's fancy hairdo was pinned with tiny pearls for the wedding.» What does fancy hairdo mean? | A hairbrush with a long handle | A cheap wig for dressing up | * A special, fancy hairstyle | A dress with lots of pearls
test: Which word fits best? «Mia had a new ___ with long curls.» | puddle | * hairdo | bicycle | shoelace
exam: Ella says, «I got a new hairdo for the party.» What does she mean? | * She got a new hairstyle | She got a new pair of shoes | She started a new school | She got a new bicycle
